# Coolify Fresh Reset & Infrastructure Clean-Sweep

We are performing a "surgical reset" of the management layer. The goal is to remove all messy, failing components (like Sentinel and corrupted Big Bear folders) and install a clean, stable Coolify (V4) instance on a dedicated new port.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Data Preservation:** Your main `postgresql` (Port 5432) and `it-inventory` data are **NOT** affected.
> **Configuration Reset:** After this, you will have a fresh, empty Coolify dashboard at `http://192.168.1.186:8010`. You will need to add your server (DeanOS) back using the SSH key once.

## Proposed Changes

### [DeanOS] Infrastructure Purge

#### [DELETE] Legacy Containers
- Stop and remove: `coolify`, `coolify-sentinel`, `big-bear-coolify-*`, `big-bear-dockhand`.

#### [DELETE] Junk Folders (Root of /DATA/AppData/)
- Clear legacy leftovers: `backups`, `databases`, `logs`, `services`, `ssh`, `webhooks-during-maintenance`.
- Purge folder: `/DATA/AppData/big-bear-coolify/`
- Purge folder: `/DATA/AppData/coolify/`

### [DeanOS] Fresh Installation

#### [NEW] [docker-compose.yml](file:///DATA/AppData/coolify-v4/docker-compose.yml)
- Create a clean `docker-compose.yml` for the latest Coolify (V4).
- **Control Port:** `8010`.
- **User:** Root-less mapping where possible for security.
- **Internal Database:** Dedicated PostgreSQL (V15) inside the compose to avoid messing with your main server.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- `ssh dean "docker ps"` -> Confirm only new Coolify and your main apps are running.
- `curl -I http://192.168.1.186:8010` -> Confirm dashboard accessibility.

### Manual Verification
- Log in to the new panel and confirm the "Messy" list is gone.
- Re-add the server once using the `deanos` SSH key.
